-- title:
--   From HTo GAdjacent Stage M1 Eq Right Shape
-- statement:
--   **Global M1 rewrite to the right-action shape.** Let `params` have a field model, let `psiBi` be a bipartite state, let `family` be an indexed polynomial family, and let `k` and `ell` be natural numbers. Put $n=k-(\ell+1)$ and define $S$, $U$, and $T$ from the recurrence weight, indexed completed outcome, and half-product operator for each sampled $q=(x,xs)$ and outcomes `g`, `gs`. Then
--   Write $\Theta$ for the parameter tuple and $F$ for the indexed family.
--   $$
--   \operatorname{fromHToGAdjacentStageM1}(\Theta,\psi_{\mathrm{bi}},F,k,\ell)
--   =\mathbb E_q\sum_g\sum_{gs}\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{\mathrm{bi}}}\left(\left(L(UTT^{\mathsf H})R(S)\right)R(U)\right),
--   $$
--
--   with $q$ uniform on $\mathbb{F}_q\times\operatorname{PointTuple}(\Theta,n)$. This is the global form of the pointwise right-action identity, obtained after summing over type classes and combining the slice-height and point-tuple averages. It is used by `fromHToGAdjacentStage_paperMoveChain` in the M1 stage of the Bernoulli move chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGAdjacentStageM1_eq_rightShape`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
